#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
analysis.py — Fixed 3-layer, process-based snowpack model
=========================================================
Task: evolve a 3-layer snowpack (data/snowpack_init.json) under 68 days of
hourly atmospheric forcing (data/forcing.csv) and write:
  results/snow_state.npy      float64 (68, 3, 5) [thickness_m, density_kg_m3, ice_mm, liq_mm, temp_K]
  results/snow_summary.csv    day, swe_mm, snow_depth_m, melt_mm, refreeze_mm, runoff_mm, mean_density_kg_m3
  results/snow_evolution.png  2x3 diagnostic figure

Formulation
-----------
* Fixed 3 layers, each isothermal (lumped). State per layer:
  W_ice, W_liq [kg/m2 == mm w.e.] (separate ice and liquid states), T [K],
  rho [kg/m3] (ice-matrix density). Thickness DERIVED: h_i = (W_ice+W_liq)/rho
  -> mass-thickness consistency exact by construction; compaction raises rho
  and thins h with W unchanged. Guards: h >= 1e-6 m, W_ice floored at 1e-6
  kg/m2 so a fully melted layer cannot produce NaN/divide-by-zero.
* Time step: 1-h forcing linearly interpolated; internal dt = 900 s (15-min
  sub-steps, 4 per hour, 6528 total). Far below conduction stability limit
  (Fo ~ 1e-3); resolves diurnal surface-balance swing controlling melt timing.
* Per sub-step: (1) deposition to top layer: snow at T_snow=min(t_air,273.15)
  as ice, fresh-snow density rho_f = 100 + 0.4*max(0, T_snow-273.15) kg/m3
  (all snowfall in this record is cold -> 100 kg/m3); layer density
  mass-weighted, reset to rho_f if layer essentially empty (<1e-3 kg/m2);
  rain (zero here) as liquid at t_air; deposition carries sensible heat.
  (2) Surface energy balance, NO degree-day shortcut: skin temperature T_s
  solved by bisection (residual monotonically decreasing in T_s):
    (1-a)*sw + lw - eps*sb*T_s^4 + h_s*(t_air-T_s) - L_v*E(T_s) + k1*(T1-T_s)/h1 = 0
  a=0.80 (aged snow, constant), eps=0.99, h_s=40 W/m2/K (no wind in forcing),
  E = k_e*(qs(T_s)-q_a), k_e=5e-3 m/s, q_a = RH*qs(t_air) with ASSUMED
  RH=0.8 (no humidity in forcing), qs Magnus. Skin has zero heat capacity:
  net flux Q = (1-a)*sw + lw - eps*sb*T_s^4 + h_s*(t_air-T_s) - L_v*E is the
  heat input to layer 1. If T_s solves above 273.15 it is capped and surplus
  melts layer-1 ice. Sublimation (E>0) removes ice mass; condensation adds
  negligible ice. Both enter the mass balance.
  (3) Inter-layer conduction: G12 = kh(k1,k2)*(T2-T1)/h12 etc., harmonic-mean
  k, mean thickness; k = 2.07e-4*rho - 1.07e-7*rho^2 W/m/K (Hutter 1986,
  floor 0.05). Bottom boundary INSULATED (no ground temperature in forcing).
  (4) Temperature update with latent-heat partitioning: C = W_ice*c_ice +
  W_liq*c_w [J/m2/K] (floor 1.0). If T_new > 273.15: melt min(W_ice,
  C*(T_new-273.15)/L_f) (counted in melt). If T_new < 273.15 with liquid:
  refreeze min(W_liq, C*(273.15-T_new)/L_f) (counted in refreeze); wet layers
  pinned at 273.15 K. L_f = 334 kJ/kg.
  (5) Compaction, Anderson & Niu (2010) functional form:
      d(rho)/dt = C_c * exp(-C2*rho/rho_ice) * sigma_overburden
  sigma = g*sum(rho_j*h_j over layers above) [Pa]; C2 = 7.834 (dimensionless);
  rho_ice = 917 kg/m3. C_c = 5e-9 m^-2 s^-1. DOCUMENTED CHOICE: exact
  published SNH constant set could not be verified offline, so the A&N
  functional form is used with C_c calibrated to field-realistic rates:
  ~0.05-0.07 kg/m3/day for the 157 and 274 kg/m3 layers under ~0.6-1.3 kPa
  overburden, zero for the unloaded top layer.
  Robustness: a top layer with total SWE < W_PASS (10 mm) is treated as an
  energy pass-through (meltout of the top layer): the surface energy balance
  acts on layer 2, percolating melt/refreeze priority still consumes the
  residual layer-1 ice first, and T1 is reported equal to T2. Per-sub-step
  |dT| is capped at DT_CAP (5 K) so thin layers cannot run away.
  (6) Liquid water / drainage: retention w_crit = 3% of layer ice SWE
  (standard percolation threshold; not in data). If a layer is at 273.15 K
  and W_liq > w_crit, the excess percolates down one layer per sub-step
  (instantaneous above threshold); into a cold layer it refreezes (latent
  heat credited). Bottom layer: excess liquid at 0 C exits as RUNOFF (bottom
  only); in a cold bottom layer percolating water refreezes instead. No
  upward redistribution.
* Mass bookkeeping: SWE(t) = sum(W_ice+W_liq); boundary terms only
  (deposition in, sublimation out, condensation in, runoff out); melt and
  refreeze are internal conversions. Closing residual asserted and printed.
* Outputs: daily snapshots at END of day d (hour 24(d+1)), d=0..67 ->
  n_days=68, all 1632 forcing hours used. melt/refreeze/runoff are DAILY
  CUMULATIVES (melt includes water that later refreezes):
  dSWE = snow + rain + cond - sub - runoff exactly. mean_density = SWE/depth.
"""
import json
import os

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
try:
    import matplotlib
    matplotlib.use("Agg")
    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
    HAVE_MPL = True
except ImportError:  # fallback: pure-numpy PNG renderer (below)
    HAVE_MPL = False

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- constants
G = 9.81                 # m/s2
L_F = 334e3              # J/kg latent heat of fusion
L_V = 2.5e6              # J/kg latent heat of vaporization
C_ICE = 2100.0           # J/kg/K
C_W = 4190.0             # J/kg/K
RHO_ICE = 917.0          # kg/m3
SIGMA_SB = 5.67e-8       # W/m2/K4
EPS = 0.99               # snow emissivity
ALBEDO = 0.80            # shortwave albedo (aged snow, constant)
H_S = 40.0               # W/m2/K sensible heat transfer coeff (no wind data)
K_E = 5e-3               # m/s aerodynamic drag coeff for sublimation
RH = 0.8                 # ASSUMED relative humidity (no humidity in forcing)
R_V = 461.5              # J/kg/K
R_D = 287.05             # J/kg/K dry air gas constant
W_CRIT_FRAC = 0.03       # liquid retention = 3% of ice SWE
C_C = 5e-9               # m^-2 s^-1 compaction pre-factor (see docstring)
C2 = 7.834               # dimensionless compaction density exponent
DT = 900.0               # s internal sub-step (15 min)
T_MELT = 273.15          # K
W_EPS = 1e-6             # kg/m2 floor for ice SWE / thickness guards
W_PASS = 10.0            # kg/m2: top layer thinner than this is an energy
                         # pass-through (no thermal identity; surface sits on
                         # layer 2) - prevents C->0 instability during meltout
DT_CAP = 5.0             # K, max |dT| per sub-step (explicit-scheme safeguard)
N_SUB = int(round(3600.0 / DT))


def q_sat(T):
    """Saturation specific humidity kg/kg (Magnus e_sat, q = e/(R_v*T))."""
    return 611.25 * np.exp(17.67 * (T - 273.15) / (T - 28.24)) / (R_V * T)


def k_cond(rho):
    """Snow thermal conductivity W/m/K (Hutter 1986), floored at 0.05."""
    return np.maximum(0.05, 2.07e-4 * rho - 1.07e-7 * rho ** 2)


def layer_h(W_ice, W_liq, rho):
    """Layer thickness from mass and density (exact mass consistency)."""
    return np.maximum((W_ice + W_liq) / rho, 1e-6)


def solve_skin(t_air, sw, lw, T1, k1, h1, rho_air):
    """Solve surface energy balance for skin T_s (bisection).

    f(T_s) = (1-a)*sw + lw - eps*sb*T_s^4 + h_s*(t_air-T_s)
             - L_v*k_e*rho_air*(qs(T_s)-RH*qs(t_air)) + k1*(T1-T_s)/h1 = 0
    f is monotonically decreasing in T_s. Returns (T_s, q_net, e_sub):
    q_net = net flux into the pack (W/m2); e_sub = sublimation rate
    kg/m2/s (>0 = mass loss from the pack).
    """
    qa = RH * q_sat(t_air)

    def f(ts):
        return ((1.0 - ALBEDO) * sw + lw - EPS * SIGMA_SB * ts ** 4
                + H_S * (t_air - ts)
                - L_V * K_E * rho_air * (q_sat(ts) - qa)
                + k1 * (T1 - ts) / h1)

    lo, hi = 240.0, T_MELT + 10.0
    flo, fhi = f(lo), f(hi)
    if flo < 0.0:                    # no sign change: root below bracket
        ts = lo
    elif fhi > 0.0:                  # root above bracket
        ts = hi
    else:
        for _ in range(80):
            mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)
            fm = f(mid)
            if (fm > 0) == (flo > 0):
                lo, flo = mid, fm
            else:
                hi = mid
        ts = 0.5 * (lo + hi)
    if ts > T_MELT:
        ts = T_MELT
    e_sub = K_E * rho_air * (q_sat(ts) - qa)
    q_net = ((1.0 - ALBEDO) * sw + lw - EPS * SIGMA_SB * ts ** 4
             + H_S * (t_air - ts) - L_V * e_sub)
    return ts, q_net, e_sub


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- load inputs
os.makedirs("results", exist_ok=True)
with open("data/snowpack_init.json") as fh:
    init = json.load(fh)
assert init["n_layers"] == 3

W_ice = np.array([l["ice_mm"] for l in init["layers"]], dtype=float)   # kg/m2
W_liq = np.array([l["liq_mm"] for l in init["layers"]], dtype=float)
T = np.array([l["temp_K"] for l in init["layers"]], dtype=float)
rho = np.array([l["density_kg_m3"] for l in init["layers"]], dtype=float)

forc = pd.read_csv("data/forcing.csv")
t_hr = forc["time_hr"].to_numpy(dtype=float)
t_air = forc["t_air_K"].to_numpy(dtype=float)
sw_in = forc["sw_in_wm2"].to_numpy(dtype=float)
lw_in = forc["lw_in_wm2"].to_numpy(dtype=float)
sf = forc["snowfall_mm_hr"].to_numpy(dtype=float)
rf = forc["rainfall_mm_hr"].to_numpy(dtype=float)
n_hours = len(forc)
n_days = int(round(n_hours / 24))

swe0 = W_ice.sum() + W_liq.sum()
print(f"Initial: SWE = {swe0:.4f} mm, depth = "
      f"{layer_h(W_ice, W_liq, rho).sum():.4f} m")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main loop
tot_snow = tot_rain = tot_sub = tot_cond = tot_runoff = 0.0
daily = np.zeros((n_days, 3, 5))
sum_melt = np.zeros(n_days)
sum_refrz = np.zeros(n_days)
sum_run = np.zeros(n_days)
d_melt = d_refrz = d_run = 0.0
edge_events = []


def receive(j, amt):
    """Refreeze or store percolating liquid in layer j."""
    global d_refrz
    if T[j] >= T_MELT - 1e-9:
        W_liq[j] += amt
        return
    C = max(W_ice[j] * C_ICE + W_liq[j] * C_W, 1.0)
    q = C * (T_MELT - T[j])
    frz = min(amt, q / L_F)
    W_ice[j] += frz
    W_liq[j] += (amt - frz)
    T[j] = T_MELT - (q - frz * L_F) / C
    d_refrz += frz


for hr in range(n_hours):
    for sub in range(N_SUB):
        t = t_hr[hr] + sub / N_SUB
        ta = np.interp(t, t_hr, t_air)
        sw = np.interp(t, t_hr, sw_in)
        lw = np.interp(t, t_hr, lw_in)
        sfmm = np.interp(t, t_hr, sf) / 3600.0 * DT   # kg/m2 this sub-step
        rfmm = np.interp(t, t_hr, rf) / 3600.0 * DT

        # 1) deposition onto top layer
        dep_heat = 0.0
        if sfmm > 0:
            tsnow = min(ta, T_MELT)
            rho_f = 100.0 + 0.4 * max(0.0, tsnow - T_MELT)
            if W_ice[0] < 1e-3:                      # (re)initialised layer
                rho[0] = rho_f
            else:
                rho[0] = (rho[0] * W_ice[0] + rho_f * sfmm) / (W_ice[0] + sfmm)
            W_ice[0] += sfmm
            dep_heat += sfmm * C_ICE * (tsnow - T[0])
            tot_snow += sfmm
        if rfmm > 0:
            W_liq[0] += rfmm
            dep_heat += rfmm * C_W * (ta - T[0])
            tot_rain += rfmm

        # 2) surface energy balance
        h = layer_h(W_ice, W_liq, rho)
        k = k_cond(rho)
        rho_air = 101325.0 / (R_D * ta)
        s = 0 if (W_ice[0] + W_liq[0]) >= W_PASS else 1   # surface layer index
        if s == 1:
            T[0] = T[1]                    # empty top layer: no thermal identity
        ts, q_net, e_sub = solve_skin(ta, sw, lw, T[s], k[s], h[s], rho_air)
        if e_sub > 0:                                 # sublimation mass loss
            wsub = min(e_sub * DT, W_ice[s] + W_liq[s])
            take_ice = min(wsub, W_ice[s])
            W_ice[s] -= take_ice
            W_liq[s] -= (wsub - take_ice)
            tot_sub += wsub
        else:                                         # condensation (negligible)
            wdep = -e_sub * DT
            W_ice[s] += wdep
            tot_cond += wdep

        # 3) inter-layer conduction (no storage node in an empty top layer)
        h12 = 0.5 * (h[0] + h[1])
        h23 = 0.5 * (h[1] + h[2])
        kh12 = 2.0 / (1.0 / k[0] + 1.0 / k[1])
        kh23 = 2.0 / (1.0 / k[1] + 1.0 / k[2])
        g12 = kh12 * (T[1] - T[0]) / h12 if s == 0 else 0.0
        g23 = kh23 * (T[2] - T[1]) / h23

        # 4) temperature update with latent-heat partitioning
        E = np.zeros(3)
        if s == 0:
            E[0] += q_net + g12 + dep_heat
            E[1] += g23 - g12
        else:
            E[1] += q_net + g23 + dep_heat
        E[2] += -g23
        E *= DT
        for i in range(3):
            if i == 0 and s == 1:
                continue                        # pass-through: no energy storage
            C = max(W_ice[i] * C_ICE + W_liq[i] * C_W, 1.0)
            dT = max(-DT_CAP, min(DT_CAP, E[i] / C))
            Tnew = T[i] + dT
            if Tnew > T_MELT:                         # melting
                q = C * (Tnew - T_MELT)
                avail = W_ice[i]
                if i == 1 and s == 1:                # residual layer-1 ice melts first
                    avail += W_ice[0]
                m = min(avail, q / L_F)
                if i == 1 and s == 1 and W_ice[0] > 0.0 and m > 0.0:
                    m0 = min(W_ice[0], m)
                    W_ice[0] -= m0
                    W_liq[0] += m0
                    m -= m0
                W_ice[i] -= m
                W_liq[i] += m
                T[i] = T_MELT
                d_melt += m
            elif Tnew < T_MELT and W_liq[i] > 0.0:    # refreezing
                q = C * (T_MELT - Tnew)
                frz = min(W_liq[i], q / L_F)
                W_liq[i] -= frz
                W_ice[i] += frz
                T[i] = T_MELT - (q - frz * L_F) / C
                d_refrz += frz
            else:
                T[i] = Tnew
            W_ice[i] = max(W_ice[i], 0.0)
            W_liq[i] = max(W_liq[i], 0.0)
        if s == 1:
            T[0] = T[1]                    # keep reported T1 in sync

        # 5) compaction (Anderson & Niu form, see docstring)
        h = layer_h(W_ice, W_liq, rho)
        sigma = np.array([0.0,
                          G * (rho[0] * h[0]),
                          G * (rho[0] * h[0] + rho[1] * h[1])])
        for i in range(3):
            if W_ice[i] > W_EPS and rho[i] < RHO_ICE and sigma[i] > 0:
                drho = C_C * np.exp(-C2 * rho[i] / RHO_ICE) * sigma[i] * DT
                rho[i] = min(rho[i] + drho, RHO_ICE)

        # 6) liquid percolation and bottom runoff
        for i in range(2):
            wcrit = W_CRIT_FRAC * W_ice[i]
            if T[i] >= T_MELT - 1e-9 and W_liq[i] > wcrit:
                excess = W_liq[i] - wcrit
                W_liq[i] -= excess
                receive(i + 1, excess)
        wcrit3 = W_CRIT_FRAC * W_ice[2]
        if T[2] >= T_MELT - 1e-9 and W_liq[2] > wcrit3:
            excess = W_liq[2] - wcrit3
            W_liq[2] -= excess
            tot_runoff += excess
            d_run += excess

        # guards / diagnostics
        if not (np.all(np.isfinite(W_ice)) and np.all(np.isfinite(W_liq))
                and np.all(np.isfinite(T)) and np.all(np.isfinite(rho))):
            raise RuntimeError(f"non-finite state at t={t} h")
        if W_ice[0] < 1e-3 and sfmm > 0:
            edge_events.append(f"t={t:.1f} h: top layer re-init on deposition")

    if hr % 24 == 23:                     # end of day -> daily snapshot
        d = hr // 24
        h = layer_h(W_ice, W_liq, rho)
        daily[d] = np.stack([h, rho, W_ice, W_liq, T], axis=1)
        sum_melt[d] = d_melt
        sum_refrz[d] = d_refrz
        sum_run[d] = d_run
        d_melt = d_refrz = d_run = 0.0
        if d % 10 == 9:
            print(f"  day {d+1:2d}: SWE={W_ice.sum()+W_liq.sum():8.3f} mm  "
                  f"depth={h.sum():.4f} m  T1={T[0]:.2f} K  melt={sum_melt[d]:.2f} mm")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mass balance
swe_end = W_ice.sum() + W_liq.sum()
residual = (swe_end - swe0 - tot_snow - tot_rain - tot_cond
            + tot_sub + tot_runoff)
print("\n--- Mass balance (mm water equivalent) ---")
print(f"  SWE initial          : {swe0:12.4f}")
print(f"  + snowfall           : {tot_snow:12.4f}")
print(f"  + rainfall           : {tot_rain:12.4f}")
print(f"  + condensation       : {tot_cond:12.6f}")
print(f"  - sublimation        : {tot_sub:12.6f}")
print(f"  - runoff             : {tot_runoff:12.4f}")
print(f"  = SWE final          : {swe_end:12.4f}")
print(f"  closing residual     : {residual:12.2e} mm")
assert abs(residual) < 1e-6, "mass balance violated"
assert daily.shape == (n_days, 3, 5) and np.all(np.isfinite(daily))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- outputs
np.save("results/snow_state.npy", daily.astype(np.float64))

swe = daily[:, :, 2] + daily[:, :, 3]                 # mm
depth = daily[:, :, 0].sum(axis=1)
mean_rho = swe.sum(axis=1) / depth
summary = pd.DataFrame({
    "day": np.arange(n_days),
    "swe_mm": swe.sum(axis=1),
    "snow_depth_m": depth,
    "melt_mm": sum_melt,
    "refreeze_mm": sum_refrz,
    "runoff_mm": sum_run,
    "mean_density_kg_m3": mean_rho,
})
summary.to_csv("results/snow_summary.csv", index=False, float_format="%.6f")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- figure
# Primary path: matplotlib (available in the native runtime). Fallback: a
# minimal pure-numpy PNG renderer producing the same 2x3 diagnostic layout
# (used only when matplotlib is unavailable, e.g. this dev venv).
_days = np.arange(n_days)
_lc = [(31, 119, 180), (255, 127, 14), (44, 160, 44)]
_lnames = ["Layer 1 (top)", "Layer 2", "Layer 3 (bottom)"]
_swe = daily[:, :, 2] + daily[:, :, 3]
_depth = daily[:, :, 0].sum(axis=1)
_mean_rho = _swe.sum(axis=1) / _depth

if HAVE_MPL:
    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(16, 9))
    fig.suptitle("3-layer snowpack evolution under 68-day forcing", fontsize=14)

    ax = axes[0, 0]
    for i in range(3):
        ax.plot(_days, _swe[:, i], color=[c / 255 for c in _lc[i]], lw=1.4, label=_lnames[i])
    ax.plot(_days, _swe.sum(axis=1), "k", lw=2.2, label="Total SWE")
    ax.set_title("Snow water equivalent"); ax.set_xlabel("Day"); ax.set_ylabel("SWE (mm)")
    ax.legend(fontsize=8); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)

    ax = axes[0, 1]
    for i in range(3):
        ax.plot(_days, daily[:, i, 0], color=[c / 255 for c in _lc[i]], lw=1.4, label=_lnames[i])
    ax.plot(_days, _depth, "k", lw=2.2, label="Total depth")
    ax.set_title("Layer thickness"); ax.set_xlabel("Day"); ax.set_ylabel("Thickness (m)")
    ax.legend(fontsize=8); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)

    ax = axes[0, 2]
    for i in range(3):
        ax.plot(_days, daily[:, i, 1], color=[c / 255 for c in _lc[i]], lw=1.4, label=_lnames[i])
    ax.set_title("Ice density"); ax.set_xlabel("Day"); ax.set_ylabel("Density (kg/m3)")
    ax.legend(fontsize=8); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)

    ax = axes[1, 0]
    for i in range(3):
        ax.plot(_days, daily[:, i, 4], color=[c / 255 for c in _lc[i]], lw=1.4, label=_lnames[i])
    ax.axhline(273.15, color="r", ls="--", lw=1, label="0 C")
    ax.set_title("Layer temperature"); ax.set_xlabel("Day"); ax.set_ylabel("Temperature (K)")
    ax.legend(fontsize=8); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)

    ax = axes[1, 1]
    ax.plot(t_hr / 24.0, t_air, "tab:purple", lw=0.8, label="Air temperature (K)")
    ax.set_xlabel("Time (days)"); ax.set_ylabel("Air temperature (K)", color="tab:purple")
    ax2 = ax.twinx()
    ax2.plot(t_hr / 24.0, sw_in, "tab:brown", lw=0.8, alpha=0.7, label="SW in (W/m2)")
    ax2.set_ylabel("Shortwave in (W/m2)", color="tab:brown")
    ax.set_title("Forcing"); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)
    h1, l1 = ax.get_legend_handles_labels(); h2, l2 = ax2.get_legend_handles_labels()
    ax.legend(h1 + h2, l1 + l2, fontsize=8)

    ax = axes[1, 2]
    ax.bar(_days, sum_melt, color="tab:red", alpha=0.7, label="Melt (mm)")
    ax.plot(_days, sum_refrz, "tab:blue", lw=1.4, label="Refreeze (mm)")
    ax.plot(_days, sum_run, "tab:gray", lw=1.4, label="Runoff (mm)")
    ax.set_title("Daily melt / refreeze / runoff"); ax.set_xlabel("Day"); ax.set_ylabel("mm w.e.")
    ax.legend(fontsize=8); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)

    fig.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0, 1, 0.97])
    fig.savefig("results/snow_evolution.png", dpi=150)
else:
    import zlib as _zlib
    import struct as _struct

    def _png_write(path, rgb):
        h, w = rgb.shape[:2]
        raw = b"".join(b"\x00" + rgb[y].tobytes() for y in range(h))

        def _chunk(tag, data):
            return (_struct.pack(">I", len(data)) + tag + data
                    + _struct.pack(">I", _zlib.crc32(tag + data) & 0xFFFFFFFF))

        with open(path, "wb") as f:
            f.write(b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n"
                    + _chunk(b"IHDR", _struct.pack(">IIBBBBB", w, h, 8, 2, 0, 0, 0))
                    + _chunk(b"IDAT", _zlib.compress(raw, 6))
                    + _chunk(b"IEND", b""))

